Stop PluginCLAP from calling host->latency->changed() from anywhere except
inside activate() -- deactivate(), onMainThread() and stateLoad() were all
still doing so directly, which clap-validator 0.4.1 rejects.

Generated against DPF commit 4238e1c7f0351bbe488d79f0899c540543ac7583
("Merge branch 'develop'", the commit pinned by AUDIOPLUGINS_DPF_GIT_TAG in
Tank/CMakeLists.txt), with dpf-clap-state-chunked-read.patch and
dpf-clap-activate-latency.patch already applied. File:
distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp.

WHAT IS BROKEN
--------------
dpf-clap-activate-latency.patch fixed activate() never reporting a plugin's
initial latency, by calling checkForLatencyChanges(true, true) +
reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded() at the end of activate(). Its own verification
notes said deactivate() "already honors [the CLAP latency contract]
correctly" -- but that was only ever exercised by Hex, whose latency never
actually changes again after the initial activate()-time report. Tank's
"anticipation" (lookahead) parameter genuinely changes the plugin's real
latency at runtime (TankPluginAdapter::run() calls setLatency() whenever the
live parameter value changes the required lookahead-delay length), so its
clap-validator run exercises call sites the Hex patch never had to.

With Tank, `44 tests run, 25 passed, 6 failed`: param-set-events,
param-set-no-cookies, param-fuzz-basic, param-fuzz-bounds,
param-fuzz-sample-accurate and param-fuzz-modulation, all failing with:

    clap_host_latency::changed
    Must only be called within 'clap_plugin::activate'

Traced with temporary fprintf instrumentation at every checkForLatencyChanges
/ reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded call site (activate(), deactivate(),
process(), onMainThread(), stateLoad()) to find the exact offending call,
rather than guessing: the sequence is (1) a process() call detects a live
latency change, takes checkForLatencyChanges()'s isActive branch, correctly
calls request_restart() and sets fLatencyChanged=true; (2) fLastKnownLatency
is now caught up, so process()'s own explicit checkForLatencyChanges(true,
false) call immediately after returns early (no new change to report); (3)
the very next host call is deactivate(), which calls
checkForLatencyChanges(false, true) -- also an early return, since
fLastKnownLatency already matches -- immediately followed by the
*unconditional* reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded(), which still sees
fLatencyChanged==true from step (1) and duly calls
host->latency->changed(fHost) right there, from inside deactivate(). That
call is what clap-validator flags: contrary to what the CLAP header comment
for latency::changed() implies ("only allowed to change if the plugin is
deactivated"), clap-validator 0.4.1's embedded host hook only accepts the
call literally inside the clap_plugin::activate() call stack, not
clap_plugin::deactivate() or any later main-thread callback.

The same unconditional reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded() was also called from
onMainThread() and from stateLoad() (both outside activate()'s call stack),
so both were latent instances of the identical bug, not yet exercised by
Tank's specific test failures but equally non-compliant.

THE FIX
-------
checkForLatencyChanges() no longer calls host->latency->changed() directly
under any circumstance -- it only ever sets the fLatencyChanged flag, and
additionally calls request_restart() while active (unchanged from before).
reportLatencyChangeIfNeeded() -- the only place that still calls changed()
directly -- is now invoked exclusively from activate(), the one call site
clap-validator has verified accepts it (per dpf-clap-activate-latency.patch).
Its calls from deactivate(), onMainThread() and stateLoad() are removed;
each of those sites still calls checkForLatencyChanges() for
fLastKnownLatency bookkeeping (and, from deactivate()/stateLoad(), so a
genuinely fresh change detected there still sets the flag and/or requests a
restart), but the flag is only ever flushed by the next activate() call,
which is always legal.

VERIFICATION
------------
clap-validator 0.4.1 against Tank.clap, before this patch (but with
dpf-clap-state-chunked-read.patch and dpf-clap-activate-latency.patch
already applied): 44 tests run, 25 passed, 6 failed, 2 warnings, 11 skipped
-- the 6 failures listed above, all "Must only be called within
'clap_plugin::activate'".

After this patch: 44 tests run, 31 passed, 0 failed, 2 warnings, 11 skipped
(verified by name: all 6 previously-failing tests now pass). The 2 remaining
warnings (process-audio-denormals timing, state-invalid-random accepting
malformed state without crashing) are unrelated to latency and pre-existing.
pluginval --strictness-level 5 on Tank.vst3 remains SUCCESS (unaffected,
VST3 has its own latency-reporting path in DPF, not touched here). Tank's
own 6 DSP unit tests (ctest) still pass unchanged.

Not reported upstream yet -- same deliberate decision as the other two
patches in this directory.

